{"ref":"BDB, אֳנִי","hw":"אֳנִי","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אֳנִי</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:11\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.11\">1 K 10:11</a></sup> & <strong>f.</strong> v <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:22\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.22\">22</a> <strong>coll. ships, fleet</strong>—abs. <a data-ref=\"I Kings 9:26\" href=\"/I_Kings.9.26\">1 K 9:26</a> +; cstr. <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:11\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.11\">10:11</a> +;—of Sol. <a data-ref=\"I Kings 9:26\" href=\"/I_Kings.9.26\">1 K 9:26</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 9:27\" href=\"/I_Kings.9.27\">27</a>; called <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳ תַרְשִׁישׁ</span> (i.e. large, sea-going vessels, such as sail to Tarshish) <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:22\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.22\">10:22</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳ חִירָם</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:11\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.11\">10:11</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:22\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.22\">22</a>; propelled by oars <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳־שַׁיִט</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 33:21\" href=\"/Isaiah.33.21\">Is 33:21</a>.","next":"BDB, אֳנִיָּה","prev":"BDB, אנה"}